  "body": "### Summary\nAs the maintainer, I want the behaviour that cloud sessions merged on unit tests alone checked by hand on the simulator, so that no unchecked behaviour reaches the first TestFlight build. **This issue blocks LOT-161 (#251).**\n\n### Context\nCloud sessions cannot run the simulator. The operator merged these PRs on CI and an adversarial review alone (2026-10-30) and tracks the hand checks here, one issue for all of them. Add new rows here instead of opening one issue per check.\n\n### Checks (iPhone 18 Pro and iPad Pro 13-inch (M5), iOS 27.0)\n\n| # | From | Check | Expected |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1a | #307 (LOT-126), CodeRabbit security thread, fixed in 6b11bf1 | **The original case:** log in, open Messages, open a conversation, then let the session become invalid **while the account stays in the app** (same `HFRSession` object, `isLoggedIn()` turns false), and refresh the list or come back to Messages. Logging out or removing the account replaces the session object and does **not** reproduce it. If it cannot be triggered by hand on the simulator, say so in the report: the unit tests then stand alone. | The conversation closes, on iPhone (stack) **and** on iPad (two columns); only the signed-out list is shown. Tests: `aSessionThatExpiresClosesTheOpenConversation`, `aRefusedSessionClosesTheOpenConversationEvenWithItsCookie`. |\n| 1b | #307 | Same, but log out from the account screen (or remove the account). | Same result: no conversation stays on screen. |\n| 2 | #303 (LOT-170) | iPhone: Plus > Réglages > Icône, then back, twice. Switch tabs and come back to Plus. | Each screen pushes and pops; Plus returns where it was left. |\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n- One short report per row on this issue (device, result). No real pseudo, message content or account data in screenshots.\n- A failed row becomes a `type: bug` issue (a `type: security` one for rows 1a/1b, reported privately per SECURITY.md) linked here, and blocks LOT-161 until fixed.\n- Close this issue when every row passes.\n\n### Related\nLOT-161 #251 (blocked by this), #322 (visual checks of LOT-119, separate), boards #166.",
